==Classical Nahuatl==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/-toːn/|[-toːn̥]|lang=nci}}

===Suffix===
{{head|head=-tōn|nci|suffix|plural|-totōn}}

# {{lb|nci|added to nouns}} A [[diminutive]] suffix; {{non-gloss definition|forms nouns denoting smallness, and rarely insignificance}}.
{{examples-right|
* {{m|nci|ahaztli||a wing}} → {{m|nci|ahaztōntli||a small wing}}</br>
* {{m|nci|chichi||a dog}} → {{m|nci|chichitōn||a small dog; lap dog}}</br>
* {{m|nci|conētl||a child}} → {{m|nci|conētōntli||a small child; young child}}
}}

====Usage notes====
* The diminutive element {{m|nci|-tōn}} is inserted between the noun stem and the absolutive or possessive ending if there is one.
* The suffix {{m|nci|-tōn}} takes the plural form {{m|nci|-tōton|-totōn(tin)}}, undergoing [[reduplication]] plus the addition of the plural suffix {{m|nci|-tin}}.
:: {{m|nci|piltōntli||small child}} → {{m|nci|pīpiltotōntin||small children}}
* If the stem does not take an [[absolutive]] suffix (i.e. ''-li'', ''-tl'' or ''-tli''), the resulting diminutive does not either, and {{m|nci|-tin}} is omitted in the plural.
:: {{m|nci|chichitōn||small dog}} → {{m|nci|chichitotōn||small dogs}}
* The same can also happen with nouns taking the absolutive {{m|nci|-in}}.
:: {{m|nci|quimichin||mouse}} → {{m|nci|quimichtōn||small mouse}}, but {{m|nci|citlālin||star}} → {{m|nci|citlāltōntli||small star}}

====Derived terms====
{{suffixsee|nci}}

