==Finnish==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fi|fiu-fin-pro|*-t'oin}}, from {{etyl|fiu-pro|fi}}. Probably related to Northern Sámi {{m|se|-heapme}} and Moksha {{l|mdf|-фтома}}.

===Suffix===
{{fi-suffix|adjective|var=tön}}

# {{non-gloss definition|Indicates lack of something}}; [[-less]].
#: [[aika]] 'time' → [[ajaton]] 'timeless'
#: [[järki]] 'sense' → [[järjetön]] 'senseless'
#: [[maku]] 'taste' → [[mauton]] 'tasteless'
#: [[ääri]] 'border' → [[ääretön]] 'infinite'

====Usage notes====
Added to the genitive singular (weak grade) stem.

====Declension====
{{fi-decl-onneton|pos=adj|-|a}}

====Antonyms====
* {{l|fi|-llinen}}

